      "factual_description": "Jazz at Lincoln Center presents The World in Swing on Friday, April 30 and Saturday, May 1, 2027 at 7:30 PM in Rose Theater. The Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra with Wynton Marsalis is joined by Iraqi oud virtuoso Naseer Shamma, Brazilian bandolim master Hamilton de Holanda, and Spanish flamenco-jazz pianist Chano Domínguez. JALC frames the program as a cross-cultural dialogue among jazz, Arab classical traditions, Brazilian music and flamenco, using traditional and original melodies as material for large-ensemble collaboration and improvisation. The engagement is part of JALC's 2026-27 Come Home season, Marsalis's final season as Artistic Director.",
